`import { randomUUID } from 'crypto'` makes this module Node-specific and can break Studio/MSW browser bundles (no Node `crypto` polyfill). Prefer `globalThis.crypto?.randomUUID()` (Web Crypto) with a small fallback implementation, and avoid importing from `crypto` in this file.
```suggestion

function randomUUID(): string {
    const cryptoObj = (typeof globalThis !== 'undefined' ? (globalThis as any).crypto : undefined);
    if (cryptoObj && typeof cryptoObj.randomUUID === 'function') {
        return cryptoObj.randomUUID();
    }
    // Fallback: RFC 4122 version 4 compliant enough for non-cryptographic IDs
    // Pattern from common UUID v4 generation snippets.
    return 'xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx'.replace(/[xy]/g, c => {
        const r = (Math.random() * 16) | 0;
        const v = c === 'x' ? r : (r & 0x3) | 0x8;
        return v.toString(16);
    });
}
```

The `catch {}` around legacy broker login will also swallow real `auth.login` failures (e.g., invalid credentials) and then return a 200 mock session, masking production errors. Only fall through to mock when the broker is truly unavailable / the action is unsupported; otherwise return an error response (or rethrow) so callers see the correct failure.
```suggestion
            } catch (error: any) {
                // Only fall through to mock when the broker is truly unavailable.
                const code = error && typeof error === 'object' ? (error as any).code : undefined;
                const statusCode =
                    error && typeof error === 'object'
                        ? (error as any).statusCode ?? (error as any).status
                        : undefined;

                const isBrokerUnavailable =
                    code === 'ECONNREFUSED' ||
                    code === 'ECONNRESET' ||
                    code === 'EHOSTUNREACH' ||
                    code === 'ENOTFOUND' ||
                    statusCode === 503;

                if (!isBrokerUnavailable) {
                    // Propagate real auth/login or other failures so callers see the correct error.
                    throw error;
                }
```
